  "readmeFile": "ReadmeNuget.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Fixed a bug in the design-time checks for scripts where the return type of a user-defined function was not resolved correctly when the function returned a built-in type (such as bool, int, or string), an array, a nullable, or a generic type. Because the return type was left unresolved, using the function's return value (for example, assigning it to a variable, passing it as an argument, or accessing a member on it) could be reported as an error even though the code is valid, and conversely some real type mismatches were missed. Only user-defined-class return types were handled before; all type forms are now resolved.",
